---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Partners"
  description="Ownpremise is licensed by its maker and deployed and operated by partners in their region. What a partner does, what we do, and how to become a partner."
>
  <section class="hero blueprint">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="num">00</span>Partners</span>
      <h1>We license the platform. Partners deploy and operate it in their region.</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 1.5rem">
        Ownpremise runs on your premises, so the people who install and operate it need to be able to
        reach them. That is why the platform is available through partners: companies in your region
        who know the local requirements and can be on site.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="num">01</span>The model</span>
        <h2>Who does what.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cards">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>What a partner does</h3>
          <ul class="list">
            <li><strong>Scoping.</strong> Requirements, deployment profile, sizing and the plan to get there.</li>
            <li><strong>Hardware.</strong> Specify, supply, or qualify what you already have.</li>
            <li><strong>Operation.</strong> Install, update, back up and monitor the instance.</li>
            <li><strong>First-line support.</strong> Your first call, in your language and your time zone.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>What we do</h3>
          <ul class="list">
            <li><strong>Build and sign</strong> the platform and every release.</li>
            <li><strong>License</strong> the platform to you, through your partner, per installation.</li>
            <li><strong>Train and support</strong> partners, as their second line.</li>
            <li><strong>Stay out of your premises.</strong> We do not need access to your instance to do any of the above.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="blueprint divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="num">02</span>Territory</span>
        <h2>One partner, one agreed territory.</h2>
        <p>
          Each partner represents the platform in an agreed territory and, where relevant, an agreed
          sector. The partner list is published here as agreements are concluded. If there is no
          partner in your region yet, tell us and we will say what the options are.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band blueprint" id="become">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="num">03</span>Become a partner</span>
      <h2>Represent Ownpremise in your region.</h2>
      <p class="measure" style="margin-top: 1.25rem">
        If you deploy and operate systems for organisations that keep sensitive data, and you want to
        represent the platform where you are, write to us. Tell us your region, what you operate today
        and the kind of customers you serve.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@stacksolveruk.com?subject=Partner%20enquiry">Become a partner</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/contact">Other ways to contact us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
  }

  .list li {
    padding: 0.6rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .list li::before {
    content: none;
  }

  .list li:first-child {
    border-top: 0;
  }

  .list strong {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
